    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1973993917424214027",
      "url": "https://x.com/dost_pagasa/status/1973993917424214027",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/dost_pagasa/status/1973993917424214027",
      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 3 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Tropical Cyclone \"PAOLO\"\nIssued at: 2:00 PM, 03 October 2025(Friday)\n\nRED WARNING LEVEL: Zambales.\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: Serious FLOODING is expected in flood-prone areas.\n\nORANGE WARNING LEVEL: Bataan.\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING is still THREATENING.\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Cavite, Batangas, Pampanga, Bulacan(Hagonoy, Paombong, Bulakan, Bocaue, Meycauayan, Marilao, Obando, Malolos, Calumpit, Balagtas, Guiguinto), Tarlac(Capas, Bamban, San Jose, Concepcion) and Nueva Ecija(Carranglan, San Jose, Lupao, Pantabangan, Bongabon, Rizal, Llanera, Munoz, Talugtug, Cuyapo).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, light to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Quezon, Laguna, Rizal, Metro Manila, Tarlac(Anao, Tarlac City, Gerona, La Paz, Paniqui, Pura, Ramos, San Manuel, Victoria, Camiling, Mayantoc, Moncada, San Clemente, Santa Ignacia), Nueva Ecija(Cabiao, Gapan, General Tinio, San Antonio, San Isidro, Aliaga, Cabanatuan, Gabaldon, General Mamerto Natividad, Guimba, Jaen, Laur, Licab, Nampicuan, Palayan, Penaranda, Quezon, San Leonardo, Santa Rosa, Santo Domingo, Talavera, Zaragoza) and Bulacan(Angat, Baliuag, Bustos, San Jose del Monte, Dona Remedios Trinidad, Norzagaray, Pandi, Plaridel, Pulilan, San Ildefonso, San Miguel, San Rafael, Santa Maria) which may persist within 3 hours.\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 5:00 PM today.\n\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
